  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper ridge over the northern plains with a cut off low in\nCalifornia resulting in continued very hot temperatures over\neastern Montana.\n\nStrong low level southeast winds will continue for at least one\nmore day of critical fire weather and significant waves on Fort\nPeck Lake. Hazard headlines remain in place for Red Flag, Lake\nWind and Heat through today.\n\nSlight modification occurs on Friday, particularly with the winds\ndiminishing, as the California low begins slowly shifting\nnortheastward. By Saturday, a more significant change in the\nweather is expected with increasing moisture and clouds, cooler\ntemperatures and chances for thunderstorms. The cooler and wetter\nconditions will continue into next week. \nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nHigh temperatures have not been meeting the forecast for many\nlocations over the past few days. Values have been closer to the\nNBM10, so adjusted MaxT for today and Friday by blending with\nNBM10.",
